<title>UK: Compass rises as DKB repeats &quot;buy&quot;.</title>
<headline>Compass rises as DKB repeats &quot;buy&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in catering firm Compass Group Plc rose 6p to 692.5p on Friday as Dresdner Kleinwort Benson repeated its &quot;buy&quot; stance.  </p>
<p>DKB analyst Greg Feehely said a recent trip to North America had underlined the potential of that market.</p>
<p>The visit coincided with the acquisition by Compass of the food service business of Daka International Inc for $195 million. Daka is a major caterer to the U.S. educational market.</p>
<p>&quot;This deal will be earnings enhancing and is of strategic importance,&quot; said Feehely.</p>
<p>&quot;These shares have been as high as 742p and this is an opportunity to buy,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Keith Weir, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
